---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About The UK Punter — How We Test & Rank Casinos"
  description="How The UK Punter tests casinos: real deposits, timed withdrawals, and UKGC-licensed operators only. Our methodology and funding explained."
>
  <article class="article-wrap">
    <h1>About The UK Punter</h1>
    <div class="article-body">
      <p>
        The UK Punter is an independent comparison site for UK players. We compare online
        casinos on the factors players actually care about — withdrawal speed, real RTP
        figures, minimum deposits, payment methods and bonus terms — and we only ever feature
        operators licensed by the <strong>UK Gambling Commission</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Our testing methodology</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Real accounts, real money.</strong> We register, deposit and withdraw with our own funds at every casino we review.</li>
        <li><strong>Timed withdrawals.</strong> Payout speeds quoted on this site are measured from withdrawal request to money arriving, not taken from the operator's marketing.</li>
        <li><strong>Terms read in full.</strong> We read the complete bonus terms and flag wagering requirements, game weightings, max bets and win caps.</li>
        <li><strong>Regular re-testing.</strong> Terms change constantly. Comparison pages display a "last updated" date and are re-checked when operators change their terms.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we make money</h2>
      <p>
        When you sign up to a casino through a link on this site, we may receive a commission
        from the operator. This never costs you anything and never changes our rankings — our
        comparison tables are ordered by measured performance, not by who pays us most. If a
        casino performs poorly in our tests, we say so.
      </p>

      <h2>Our commitment to safer gambling</h2>
      <p>
        We believe honest information makes gambling safer. Every page on this site links to
        free support services, and we explain restrictions like stake limits and affordability
        checks factually — because informed players make better decisions. If gambling has
        stopped being fun, visit our <a href="/responsible-gambling/">responsible gambling page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
